WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.761 --> 00:00:04.186
What do I think about Zazzle?

00:00:04.581 --> 00:00:06.111
So I got a great question from one of my

00:00:06.111 --> 00:00:07.851
Google + viewers William

00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:09.803
(love you guys!) who wrote in to say

00:00:10.472 --> 00:00:12.565
“Hello Evan. I would really like to hear your opinion

00:00:12.728 --> 00:00:15.893
on Print On Demand websites such as Zazzle and Spreadshirt.

00:00:15.893 --> 00:00:18.415
I see a lot of artists and entrepreneurs using their services.

00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:21.364
I personally have decided to go down a different path

00:00:21.364 --> 00:00:23.754
because for me I feel it’s not the right way to do business.

00:00:24.222 --> 00:00:26.379
But I think it would make for an interesting discussion

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:28.626
if you can give your thoughts on it.”

00:00:28.626 --> 00:00:31.377
So William, this will be an interesting discussion

00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:33.838
unfortunately one-way because… you know

00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:34.992
unless you want to make a video response

00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:36.366
I’d love to see that.

00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:38.491
But I’m actually a fan of Zazzle and I’ll tell you why.

00:00:38.615 --> 00:00:39.328
You’re not going to make

00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:41.401
millions of dollars selling stuff on Zazzle

00:00:41.521 --> 00:00:43.526
okay, but that’s not the point.

00:00:43.526 --> 00:00:46.325
The point of Zazzle is to help you get started.

00:00:46.325 --> 00:00:48.046
This is why you use Zazzle.

00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:50.230
It’s to help you launch your business.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.343
If you’re trying to launch a t-shirt line

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:54.643
okay, say you want to launch a new brand of t-shirts

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:57.355
the way that most entrepreneurs will go about it is

00:00:57.621 --> 00:00:59.673
you have to go and buy t-shirts, right.

00:00:59.673 --> 00:01:01.961
You have to stock up on inventory.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.253
So you create your design and then you have to go

00:01:04.253 --> 00:01:06.433
and get men’s and women’s

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.613
from extra small to XXXL

00:01:08.613 --> 00:01:10.794
and you’re carrying lots of inventory.

00:01:10.794 --> 00:01:12.167
If you’re waiting for an order to come

00:01:12.277 --> 00:01:13.808
and then you’re going to go put out that order

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:15.194
right, like some guy comes and says

00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:17.214
“Hey, I like that shirt, I want to buy one”

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:18.363
you got to go print one

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:20.452
that’s going to be super expensive for you.

00:01:20.452 --> 00:01:22.073
You’re not going to make any money off it.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.831
So the way to make money is to sell a thousand of them

00:01:24.831 --> 00:01:26.412
5 thousand of them, 10 thousand of them.

00:01:26.412 --> 00:01:29.804
Make that kind of order because then the cost per shirt

00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:32.221
comes down to a price where you can make money.

00:01:32.432 --> 00:01:35.598
But, this is the big but, the big problem

00:01:36.661 --> 00:01:39.589
– it’s that you don’t know which shirt’s going to sell or not.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:43.478
And so many people take the little money that they have right,

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:45.071
I’m assuming money is important to you

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.667
you don’t have a ton of reserves built up

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:48.969
you can’t blow this cash

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:52.520
whatever money you spend has to pay off, right

00:01:52.521 --> 00:01:55.713
they blow their money on that first run

00:01:55.971 --> 00:01:59.472
that first line, and then it doesn’t sell.

00:01:59.802 --> 00:02:02.784
And you’re stuck with all these shirts sitting in your garage.

00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:07.471
So why I love Zazzle is because it allows you to test out

00:02:07.471 --> 00:02:11.199
your concept without spending any money on it. Right

00:02:12.229 --> 00:02:13.957
you may have 20 designs for shirt ideas.

00:02:14.361 --> 00:02:16.322
Maybe 2 of them will be amazing

00:02:16.322 --> 00:02:17.657
and the other 18 won’t work out

00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:19.358
but you don’t know until you test.

00:02:19.358 --> 00:02:20.741
You may think they’re all amazing.

00:02:20.971 --> 00:02:22.261
You got to see what the market wants too.

00:02:22.943 --> 00:02:25.655
So Zazzle allows you to put them online, right.

00:02:25.655 --> 00:02:28.384
You put them online, you may make a dollar a shirt

00:02:28.561 --> 00:02:30.321
you may make 50 cents a shirt – it doesn’t matter.

00:02:30.321 --> 00:02:32.454
What you’re doing is testing the concept

00:02:32.454 --> 00:02:36.431
and also building a customer base.

00:02:36.735 --> 00:02:37.632
So you put them online

00:02:37.632 --> 00:02:39.536
you promote them like you would promote your regular shirts

00:02:39.536 --> 00:02:41.043
and you see what does well.

00:02:41.043 --> 00:02:42.505
If you can sell a hundred shirts on Zazzle

00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:47.336
now you can talk about having justification to go out

00:02:47.336 --> 00:02:49.069
and create an order, right

00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:51.888
and spend money to buy a thousand shirts

00:02:51.888 --> 00:02:53.600
where you can start making some money.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.740
But if you can’t sell a hundred shirts on Zazzle

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:01.061
then why would you go out and order a thousand shirts?

00:03:01.061 --> 00:03:02.281
You’re going to lose your money on it.

00:03:03.174 --> 00:03:04.867
So I love Zazzle for early stage

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:05.769
for proving concept

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:08.627
for showing that this thing works

00:03:08.627 --> 00:03:09.662
that people actually care

00:03:09.662 --> 00:03:11.955
that people actually buy your product

00:03:12.676 --> 00:03:14.614
and then taking the winning ideas

00:03:14.614 --> 00:03:16.342
and going out and launching a line with that.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:17.937
That’s why I love Zazzle.

00:03:18.694 --> 00:03:19.634
Believe.

